{
  "program": "M2ENC",
  "title": "MIDTERM II REFERENCE",
  "sections": [
    {
      "menu": "JOINT LAWS",
      "title": "JOINT DISTRIBUTIONS",
      "topics": [
        {
          "menu": "PMF AND PDF",
          "title": "PMF AND PDF",
          "pages": [
            [
              "PMF p(x,y)=P(X=x,Y=y). All",
              "weights nonnegative; sum",
              "over every allowed pair",
              "=1.",
              "PDF f(x,y)≥0 and integral",
              "over support S =1. A",
              "density value can exceed1.",
              "Point probabilities are0",
              "for joint densities."
            ],
            [
              "If p=cq, c=1/sum(q). If",
              "f=cq, c=1/integral(q).",
              "Check nonnegativity too.",
              "Freund Ch3 S5 pp82-91.",
              "TOOL DISCRETE or DENSITY."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "menu": "MARGINALS",
          "title": "MARGINALS",
          "pages": [
            [
              "pX(x)=sum_y p(x,y).",
              "pY(y)=sum_x p(x,y). Keep",
              "the named variable; remove",
              "the other.",
              "fX(x)=integral f(x,y)dy",
              "over allowed y for that x.",
              "fY(y)=integral f(x,y)dx",
              "over allowed x for that y.",
              "On 0<x<y<1, fX uses y=x..1"
            ],
            [
              "and fY uses x=0..y. State",
              "support and zero",
              "elsewhere.",
              "Freund Ch3 S6 pp92-95."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "menu": "CONDITIONAL LAWS",
          "title": "CONDITIONAL LAWS",
          "pages": [
            [
              "p(X=x|Y=y)=p(x,y)/pY(y).",
              "f(X=x|Y=y)=f(x,y)/fY(y)",
              "means a density.",
              "The denominator belongs to",
              "the GIVEN variable and",
              "must be positive. Hold",
              "that value fixed; use its",
              "support slice.",
              "The conditional sums or"
            ],
            [
              "integrates to1. For",
              "continuous Y, P(Y=y)=0;",
              "use densities, not",
              "probability division by0.",
              "Joint=conditional*matching",
              "marginal. Two marginals",
              "alone leave dependence",
              "unknown.",
              "Freund Ch3 S7 pp95-101."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "menu": "CDF CONVERSIONS",
          "title": "CDF CONVERSIONS",
          "pages": [
            [
              "F(x,y)=P(X≤x,Y≤y). Sum",
              "masses or integrate",
              "density over the",
              "lower-left rectangle",
              "intersected with support.",
              "f(x,y)=mixed derivative of",
              "F for an absolutely",
              "continuous law.",
              "FX(x)=limit of F(x,y) as y"
            ],
            [
              "grows.",
              "Rectangle probability =",
              "F(b,d) - F(a,d) - F(b,c) +",
              "F(a,c).",
              "Integer-inclusive lower",
              "endpoints a,c need",
              "a-1,c-1. Noninteger",
              "supports use left limits.",
              "Give all CDF branches;"
            ],
            [
              "stop integrating at",
              "support edges."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "menu": "INDEPENDENCE",
          "title": "INDEPENDENCE",
          "pages": [
            [
              "Independent iff",
              "F(x,y)=FX(x)*FY(y) for",
              "every x,y. PMFs factor at",
              "every pair. PDFs factor",
              "almost everywhere.",
              "Compare the SUPPORT too.",
              "Product positive on a",
              "region where joint density",
              "is0 disproves"
            ],
            [
              "independence.",
              "Independent => conditional",
              "equals marginal;",
              "E[g(X)h(Y)]=E[g(X)]E[h(Y)]",
              "when integrable.",
              "One agreeing pair never",
              "proves independence.",
              "Numerical spot checks do",
              "not establish a density"
            ],
            [
              "identity."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "menu": "BOUNDS AND WORDS",
          "title": "BOUNDS AND WORDS",
          "pages": [
            [
              "Draw support S and event",
              "A. Integrate on S",
              "intersect A. Outer limits",
              "are constants; inner",
              "limits may depend on outer",
              "variable.",
              "X<Y means y>x. X+Y≤b means",
              "y≤b-x. Split wherever a",
              "boundary changes."
            ],
            [
              "Series device fails if",
              "either fails. T=min(X,Y).",
              "P(T≤t)=1-P(X>t,Y>t).",
              "Parallel device fails",
              "after both fail.",
              "T=max(X,Y). P(T≤t)=F(t,t).",
              "Independence is needed to",
              "multiply survivals."
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "menu": "EXPECT + MOMENTS",
      "title": "EXPECT AND MOMENTS",
      "topics": [
        {
          "menu": "EXPECTATION",
          "title": "EXPECTATION",
          "pages": [
            [
              "E[X]=sum x*p(x), or",
              "integral x*f(x)dx over",
              "support. It is a weighted",
              "average, not necessarily a",
              "possible observed value.",
              "Finite expectation",
              "requires E[abs(X)] finite.",
              "Symmetry cannot rescue a",
              "divergent expectation."
            ],
            [
              "The calculator averages",
              "values with weights",
              "automatically. Check model",
              "and support first.",
              "Freund Ch4 S2 pp113-121."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "menu": "LOTUS g(X,Y)",
          "title": "LOTUS g(X,Y)",
          "pages": [
            [
              "E[g(X)]=sum g(x)p(x), or",
              "integral g(x)f(x)dx. No",
              "need to derive a",
              "transformed distribution",
              "first.",
              "For g(X,Y), average g",
              "against the JOINT law. A",
              "sum of marginal",
              "expectations cannot"
            ],
            [
              "determine general",
              "products.",
              "For Y=X², E[Y]=E[X²],",
              "E[Y²]=E[X^4].",
              "Var(Y)=E[X^4]-E[X²]².",
              "TOOL FUNCTION g(X,Y) or",
              "FUNCTION g(X)."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "menu": "LINEARITY",
          "title": "LINEARITY",
          "pages": [
            [
              "E[aX+bY+c]=aE[X]+bE[Y]+c.",
              "No independence is",
              "required.",
              "E[g(X)] usually differs",
              "from g(E[X]). E[X²]",
              "usually differs from",
              "E[X]².",
              "If X≤Y then E[X]≤E[Y] when",
              "expectations exist."
            ],
            [
              "E[1_EVENT]=P(EVENT).",
              "A product factors only",
              "under suitable",
              "independence. Expand",
              "polynomial payoffs before",
              "taking expectations."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "menu": "RAW MOMENTS",
          "title": "RAW MOMENTS",
          "pages": [
            [
              "Raw rth moment mR=E[X^r].",
              "m0=1; m1=mean; m2=second",
              "raw moment.",
              "Use sum x^r*p(x), or",
              "integral x^r*f(x)dx.",
              "Existing odd moments",
              "vanish for symmetry",
              "about0.",
              "Mean requires first"
            ],
            [
              "moment. Variance needs",
              "second moment. Variance of",
              "X² needs fourth moment.",
              "TOOL PRODUCT MOMENTS with",
              "y-power0, or RAW/CENTRAL",
              "in DENSITY."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "menu": "CENTRAL MOMENTS",
          "title": "CENTRAL MOMENTS",
          "pages": [
            [
              "Central rth",
              "moment=E[(X-M)^r] with",
              "M=E[X]. First central",
              "moment0. Second central",
              "moment=variance.",
              "Var(X)=E[X²]-M² ≥0.",
              "SD=sqrt(Var). A zero",
              "variance means X constant",
              "almost surely."
            ],
            [
              "mu3=m3-3*M*m2+2*M³. mu4 =",
              "m4 - 4*M*m3 + 6*M²*m2 -",
              "3*M^4.",
              "Mean has original units;",
              "variance has squared",
              "units."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "menu": "SHIFT SCALE",
          "title": "SHIFT SCALE",
          "pages": [
            [
              "E[aX+b]=aM+b.",
              "Var(aX+b)=a²*Var(X).",
              "SD(aX+b)=abs(a)*SD(X).",
              "A shift changes mean but",
              "not variance. Negative",
              "scaling reverses direction",
              "but SD stays nonnegative.",
              "Z=(X-M)/SD has mean0 and",
              "variance1 if SD>0."
            ],
            [
              "Standardizing alone does",
              "not make a law normal.",
              "Freund Ch4 S3 pp121-125."
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "menu": "MGFS",
      "title": "MOMENT GENERATING",
      "topics": [
        {
          "menu": "DEF AND DOMAIN",
          "title": "DEF AND DOMAIN",
          "pages": [
            [
              "M(t)=E[e^(tX)]. Discrete",
              "sum e^(tx)p(x); continuous",
              "integral e^(tx)f(x)dx. The",
              "surviving variable is t.",
              "M(0)=1. Standard moment",
              "and uniqueness theorems",
              "need M finite on an OPEN",
              "interval containing0.",
              "For rate L>0 exponential"
            ],
            [
              "density L*e^(-Lx),",
              "M(t)=L/(L-t), t<L.",
              "A numerical finite cutoff",
              "cannot prove convergence",
              "on an infinite interval.",
              "Freund Ch4 S5 pp127-131."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "menu": "MOMENT DERIVS",
          "title": "MOMENT DERIVS",
          "pages": [
            [
              "M^(r)(0)=E[X^r].",
              "Mean=Mprime(0). Second",
              "moment=Msecond(0).",
              "Variance = Msecond(0) -",
              "Mprime(0)².",
              "In a Taylor series",
              "multiply coefficient of",
              "t^r by r! to obtain the",
              "raw moment."
            ],
            [
              "K(t)=ln M(t).",
              "Kprime(0)=mean.",
              "Ksecond(0)=variance.",
              "Generic numerical MGF",
              "tools APPROXIMATE",
              "derivatives. Compare two",
              "step sizes and keep stable",
              "digits; derive exact",
              "answers by hand."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "menu": "AFFINE AND SUMS",
          "title": "AFFINE AND SUMS",
          "pages": [
            [
              "For Z=aX+b,",
              "MZ(t)=e^(bt)*MX(at).",
              "Change EVERY old t",
              "argument to a*t.",
              "For Z=(X-c)/d,",
              "MZ(t)=e^(-ct/d)*MX(t/d). d",
              "must be nonzero.",
              "The new domain requires",
              "a*t in the old domain."
            ],
            [
              "Negative a reverses",
              "inequalities.",
              "Independent sum => product",
              "of MGFs. Weighted sum =>",
              "product MXi(ai*t), times",
              "e^(bt) for offset."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "menu": "UNIQUENESS",
          "title": "UNIQUENESS",
          "pages": [
            [
              "Equal finite MGFs on a",
              "neighborhood of0 imply",
              "equal distributions. They",
              "do not imply the two",
              "variables are independent.",
              "Matching only means and",
              "variances does not",
              "identify the distribution.",
              "e^(A*t+B*t²) has mean A"
            ],
            [
              "and variance2B for B≥0. If",
              "B<0 it cannot be an MGF",
              "near0.",
              "Rate L exponential has",
              "mean1/L, second",
              "moment2/L², variance1/L²."
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "menu": "PRODUCT + CORR",
      "title": "PRODUCT MOMENTS",
      "topics": [
        {
          "menu": "COVARIANCE",
          "title": "COVARIANCE",
          "pages": [
            [
              "Raw product moment",
              "E[X^r*Y^s] uses the joint",
              "law. Central product",
              "moment uses centered",
              "factors.",
              "Cov(X,Y)=E[XY]-E[X]E[Y].",
              "Cov(X,X)=Var(X).",
              "Cov(X,Y)=Cov(Y,X).",
              "Cov(aX+b,cY+d) ="
            ],
            [
              "a*c*Cov(X,Y). Added",
              "constants vanish. Nonzero",
              "covariance disproves",
              "independence.",
              "Freund Ch4 S6 pp131-135."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "menu": "CORRELATION",
          "title": "CORRELATION",
          "pages": [
            [
              "rho = Cov(X,Y) /",
              "(SD(X)*SD(Y)). Requires",
              "positive finite variances.",
              "It lies between-1 and1.",
              "abs(Cov)≤SD(X)*SD(Y). An",
              "input violating this bound",
              "is impossible.",
              "Corr(aX+b,cY+d) =",
              "sign(a*c)*rho for nonzero"
            ],
            [
              "a,c. Positive scale",
              "changes leave rho",
              "unchanged.",
              "If Y=aX+b, rho=sign(a).",
              "Correlation0 means no",
              "linear covariance, not",
              "absence of dependence.",
              "BT Ch4 S4.5; Freund Ch6",
              "S7."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "menu": "ZERO NOT INDEP",
          "title": "ZERO NOT INDEP",
          "pages": [
            [
              "Thm12 p134. Independent =>",
              "E(XY)=E(X)E(Y), so σXY=0.",
              "The converse is FALSE.",
              "Ex17 p135. f(-1,-1)=1/6,",
              "f(0,-1)=1/3, f(1,-1)=1/6,",
              "f(-1,1)=1/6, f(1,1)=1/6,",
              "all other pairs 0.",
              "μX=0, μY=-1/3, μ'1,1=0, so",
              "σXY=0-0*(-1/3)=0."
            ],
            [
              "But f(-1,-1)=1/6 while",
              "g(-1)h(-1)=(1/3)(2/3)=2/9.",
              "One failing pair =>",
              "dependent.",
              "Covariance measures only",
              "LINEAR association."
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "menu": "LINEAR COMBOS",
      "title": "ONE AND TWO COMBOS",
      "topics": [
        {
          "menu": "ONE COMBINATION",
          "title": "ONE COMBINATION",
          "pages": [
            [
              "W=c+sum ai*Xi. Mean=c+sum",
              "ai*mean_i.",
              "Var(W)=sum ai²*Var_i",
              "+2*sum i<j ai*aj*Cov_ij.",
              "With3 variables include",
              "XY,XZ,YZ pairs once each",
              "with factor2. Keep signs",
              "in cross terms.",
              "Independence OR zero"
            ],
            [
              "pairwise covariances",
              "removes cross terms.",
              "Constants add no variance.",
              "Freund Ch4 S7 pp136-138."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "menu": "TWO COMBINATIONS",
          "title": "TWO COMBINATIONS",
          "pages": [
            [
              "U=sum ai*Xi+c, V=sum",
              "bi*Xi+d. Cov(U,V)=sum_i",
              "sum_j ai*bj*Cov(Xi,Xj).",
              "For U=aX+bY,V=cX+dY,",
              "Cov=ac*VarX+bd*VarY",
              "+(ad+bc)*CovXY.",
              "Shared inputs can make",
              "combinations dependent",
              "even if original variables"
            ],
            [
              "are independent.",
              "Corr(U,V) = Cov(U,V) /",
              "sqrt(VarU*VarV). TOOL",
              "LINEAR COMBOS."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "menu": "MATRIX SHORTCUT",
          "title": "MATRIX SHORTCUT",
          "pages": [
            [
              "Put variances on",
              "covariance matrix diagonal",
              "and covariances",
              "symmetrically off",
              "diagonal. Call it [A].",
              "Put coefficient rows into",
              "[B]. Ignore additive",
              "constants for",
              "variance/covariance."
            ],
            [
              "[B]*[A]*transpose([B])",
              "gives the output",
              "covariance matrix. One row",
              "=> one variance.",
              "Transpose is MATRIX MATH",
              "superscript T token, not",
              "alpha T. Manual matrix",
              "work is an alternative to",
              "the guided app."
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "menu": "CONDITION + HELP",
      "title": "CONDITIONING AND HELP",
      "topics": [
        {
          "menu": "CONDITIONAL MEAN",
          "title": "CONDITIONAL MEAN",
          "pages": [
            [
              "E[g(X)|Y=y] averages g",
              "using conditional weights",
              "or density at fixed y.",
              "Equivalent ratio =",
              "integral g(x)f(x,y)dx /",
              "fY(y). Sum version for a",
              "PMF. Denominator must be",
              "positive.",
              "Use the conditional slice"
            ],
            [
              "support. E[X|Y=y]=m(y) is",
              "a number; E[X|Y]=m(Y) is a",
              "random variable.",
              "SOLVERS > DENSITY+INTEGRAL",
              "> JOINT SLICE evaluates",
              "marginal and conditional",
              "quantities at any valid",
              "given value."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "menu": "CONDITIONAL VAR",
          "title": "CONDITIONAL VAR",
          "pages": [
            [
              "Let m=E[X|Y=y] and",
              "q=E[X²|Y=y]. Conditional",
              "variance=q-m².",
              "Equivalent centered",
              "integral E[(X-m)²|Y=y]",
              "often avoids subtracting",
              "similar numbers.",
              "Independence makes every",
              "conditional law equal its"
            ],
            [
              "marginal. A constant",
              "conditional mean by itself",
              "does not prove",
              "independence.",
              "Freund Ch4 S8 pp138-140."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "menu": "TOTAL LAWS",
          "title": "TOTAL LAWS",
          "pages": [
            [
              "Supplement from BT S4.3.",
              "E[X]=E[E[X|Y]].",
              "Var(X)=E[Var(X|Y)]",
              "+Var(E[X|Y]).",
              "First term is average",
              "within-group spread;",
              "second is between-mean",
              "spread.",
              "These formulas help"
            ],
            [
              "recover marginal moments",
              "from conditional models.",
              "They do not replace the",
              "direct normalization step."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "menu": "CHOOSE A SOLVER",
          "title": "CHOOSE A SOLVER",
          "pages": [
            [
              "From SOLVERS, finite",
              "values => DISCRETE TABLE.",
              "FORMULA/GRID takes",
              "x-list,y-list,weight",
              "formula. Use y-list{0} for",
              "one variable. No need",
              "normalize first.",
              "PDF with finite interval",
              "or conditional slice =>"
            ],
            [
              "DENSITY+INTEGRAL, 1D.",
              "Joint PDF with explicit",
              "inner/outer bounds =>",
              "DOUBLE INTEGRAL. Split",
              "regions at boundary",
              "changes.",
              "Given",
              "variances/covariances =>",
              "LINEAR COMBOS. Given MGF"
            ],
            [
              "=> MGF TOOLS. Derivations",
              "=> ENCYCLOPEDIA."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "menu": "INPUT AND LIMITS",
          "title": "INPUT AND LIMITS",
          "pages": [
            [
              "Programs use A-Z, theta,",
              "strings and custom M2",
              "lists. Existing graph",
              "equations and L1-L6 are",
              "not edited.",
              "Enter expression tokens",
              "normally. X,Y are",
              "random-variable arguments;",
              "A can hold a fixed"
            ],
            [
              "parameter in 1D slices.",
              "No symbolic algebra",
              "engine. Numerical",
              "integration and derivative",
              "outputs are",
              "approximations.",
              "HELP > FIND MY SOLVER",
              "starts with your given",
              "data and target. SOLVERS"
            ],
            [
              "uses your current model.",
              "HOMEWORK PRACTICE examples",
              "are for study only. Use",
              "BACK to exit. ENTER next;",
              "LEFT previous; CLEAR menu",
              "in reference pages. Check",
              "your CE before relying on",
              "it."
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
